    "custom_home_testimonials_hpAUPY": {
      "type": "custom-home-testimonials",
      "blocks": {
        "testimonial_5VFqLj": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>I bought it for the family and ended up keeping one pack at work. That is the advantage of the three-pack. The bhujia itself is beautifully crisp and surprisingly light. Excellent with afternoon tea.</p>",
            "name": "Dhruv Mehta",
            "location": "Surat"
          }
        },
        "testimonial_OrhowB": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>In our house, something crunchy always appears when people sit down together. We opened this when friends came over and everyone had an opinion about bhujia. By the end, everyone was eating from the same tin. That probably says enough.</p>",
            "name": "Ayesha Mirchandani",
            "location": "Mumbai"
          }
        },
        "testimonial_nYFRJ6": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>We opened one pack thinking the other two would last. They didn’t. It has that wonderful combination of being fine and crisp without feeling too sharp or oily. Very easy to put on the table for everyone.</p>",
            "name": "Mihir Patel",
            "location": "Ahmedabad"
          }
        },
        "testimonial_ENGKOk": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>My mother tasted it first and immediately asked where it was from. That was probably my favourite reaction. There is something very old-school about the flavour, but the overall experience feels beautifully refined.</p>",
            "name": "Rhea Advani",
            "location": "Pune"
          }
        },
        "testimonial_COXMru": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>The test for me was whether it reminded me of the bhujia we would bring back from Bikaner. It did. Not because it was excessively spicy, but because the moth and masala had that depth I associate with the real thing.</p>",
            "name": "Nandini Rathi",
            "location": "Jodhpur"
          }
        },
        "testimonial_adyTR0": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>I grew up eating bhujia in Rajasthan, so there is a certain taste you instinctively look for. This has that familiar moth flavour, but what stayed with me was how light and balanced it felt. It reminded me of home without trying too hard.</p>",
            "name": "Radhika Daga",
            "location": "Jaipur"
          }
        },
        "testimonial_q3BnjD": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>It reminded me of visiting relatives in Rajasthan and finding a tin of bhujia already waiting on the table. There is a comfort to this flavour that is difficult to describe unless you have grown up around it.</p>",
            "name": "Aakanksha Bhandari",
            "location": "Chennai"
          }
        },
        "testimonial_eG1vp8": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>We have eaten Bikaneri bhujia all our lives, which also makes us difficult customers. This tasted familiar, but much more considered. The spice, the fineness and especially the clean finish stood out.</p>",
            "name": "Raghav Agarwal",
            "location": "Kolkata"
          }
        },
        "testimonial_HEJRWM": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>What I appreciated most was the restraint. Nothing overwhelms you. You can taste the moth, the spices are beautifully measured, and it doesn’t leave that heavy feeling afterwards. It is the kind of bhujia you keep going back to.</p>",
            "name": "Rishika Jain",
            "location": "New Delhi"
          }
        },
        "testimonial_o4J41Z": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>I like snacks where the spice doesn’t overpower everything else. This is beautifully balanced and remarkably light for bhujia. You start with a small handful and somehow find yourself opening the tin again.</p>",
            "name": "Niyati Jain",
            "location": "Ahmedabad"
          }
        }
